# 42. SECURITY

Implement:

* authentication
* secure session management
* encrypted secrets where possible
* role/permission system for tools
* audit log
* confirmation dialogs
* command allowlist
* path restrictions
* localhost binding by default

The AI must NOT be allowed to execute arbitrary destructive shell commands by default.

Dangerous commands should require explicit confirmation.

Examples:

```text
rm
format
del
disk operations
registry modifications
credential extraction
```

must never be silently executed.

